WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.182
RIGHT JOIN is valid PostgreSQL syntax and it
preserves every row from

00:00:04.208 --> 00:00:09.586
the right table In this example departments is on
the right so

00:00:09.599 --> 00:00:13.336
every department remains even if no medical staff
member belongs to it

00:00:14.273 --> 00:00:19.809
For an unmatched department the staff columns will
be NULL Run

00:00:19.836 --> 00:00:24.049
the query and look for the department with no staff
That row

00:00:24.062 --> 00:00:29.826
demonstrates why the RIGHT JOIN was used In practice
many analysts

00:00:29.839 --> 00:00:33.353
prefer LEFT JOIN because it reads naturally from
left to right put

00:00:33.379 --> 00:00:37.366
the population you want to preserve first then join
optional information to

00:00:37.379 --> 00:00:41.895
it The same logic could be rewritten by placing
departments first and

00:00:41.921 --> 00:00:47.696
using LEFT JOIN to medical staff The important goal
is not preferring

00:00:47.709 --> 00:00:52.738
one keyword The important goal is making the
preserved population obvious to

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.646
the next person who reads the query
